Chapter: BvtTableCups
  cites Uoaix chapter TavernBoard
  cites Uoaix chapter WalkMap
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-178: every backgammon set's cups stand one tile either side of its board along one axis, and the sets whose
 mirrored cup stood off the STATICS0.MUL table top run along their table: 1534,1431, 1807,2805, 2043,2777 and 2467,400
 along y, 2674,2238 along x, and 2903,915 is the middle of its three-tile table. A set with no offset puts both cups on
 the board's own tile.
  btcu-line : TbdSet -> Boolean
  btcu-line (s) = walk-abs s.dx + walk-abs s.dy == 1 & tbd-cup-x s 0 + tbd-cup-x s 1 == s.x * 2 & tbd-cup-y s 0 + tbd-cup-y s 1 == s.y * 2
  btcu-all : List TbdSet, Integer -> Boolean
  btcu-all (sets) (i) = if i >= list-length sets then True else btcu-line (list-at sets i) & btcu-all sets (i + 1)
  btcu-at : List TbdSet, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  btcu-at (sets) (i) (x) (y) (dx) (dy) = let s = list-at sets i in s.x == x & s.y == y & s.dx == dx & s.dy == dy
  bvt-table-cups : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-table-cups (unused) = act
    a <- bvt-check "every backgammon set has a cup one tile either side of its board, and the six off-table sets run along their table (UOAIX-178)" (let sets = tbd-sets in list-length sets == 22 & btcu-all sets 0
      & btcu-at sets 6 1534 1431 0 1 & btcu-at sets 11 1807 2805 0 1 & btcu-at sets 15 2043 2777 0 1 & btcu-at sets 16 2467 400 0 1
      & btcu-at sets 18 2674 2238 1 0 & btcu-at sets 19 2903 915 0 -1)
    b <- bvt-check "a set with no offset fails the line test: both its cups would stand on the board" (let s = tbd-set 1497 1687 26 0 0 in not (btcu-line s) & tbd-cup-x s 0 == s.x & tbd-cup-y s 1 == s.y)
    a + b
  end
